>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>"Lost souls" and "rebels": a challenge to the assumption that low self-esteem and unhealthy lifestyles are related"</article-title><source>Health Education</source><year>1997</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>161</fpage><lpage>167</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1108/09654289710172450</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>West</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Health inequalities in the early years: Is there equalisation in youth?</article-title><source>Social Science &#x00026; Medicine</source><year>1997</year><volume>44</volume><fpage>833</fpage><lpage>858</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9080566</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0277-9536(96)00188-8</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nonnemaker</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>McNeely</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Blum</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Public and private domains of religiosity and adolescent health risk behaviors: Evidence from the National Longitudinal Study of Adolescent Health</article-title><source>Social Science &#x00026; Medicine</source><year>2003</year><volume>57</volume><fpage>2049</fpage><lpage>2054</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14512236</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0277-9536(03)00096-0</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>